  "description": "The intended audience is individuals who are exposed to or share antisemitic content online, particularly those who may be influenced by or sympathetic to antisemitic tropes and conspiracy theories. The meme leverages the popular 'Shiba Inu' meme culture to make the hateful message more palatable or shareable, targeting users familiar with internet meme formats. The audience is likely to include those who engage with or spread misinformation, hate speech, or conspiracy theories, particularly those who may be predisposed to antisemitic beliefs or who are unaware of the harmful nature of the content. The meme's design, using a cute dog to imply victimhood, is intended to evoke an emotional response that may be misattributed to the targeted group (Jews), thereby appealing to those who may be seeking simplistic explanations for complex social issues or who are influenced by antisemitic narratives.",
